WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.829 --> 00:00:07.859
Three years ago, we organized a Nexus conference
entitled 'The Triumph of Science', and we

00:00:07.859 --> 00:00:13.180
also had people from the world of transhumanism.

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:23.820
I was fascinated by the fact that, based on
a pretty pessimistic view of human nature,

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:34.830
they think that, with the technology we have,
we should improve human beings with this technology,

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:36.750
because the world is too dangerous.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:45.970
There are, indeed, nuclear weapons, and to
make sure that tragedies do not happen we

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:50.580
should use new technologies to improve human
nature.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:51.629
What do you think about that?

00:00:51.629 --> 00:00:52.640
I'm very sceptical.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:58.440
First of all, I am sceptical that we need
to re-engineer humans to achieve peace.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:03.080
Canada and the United States have not fought
a war since the War of 1812, and no one had

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:05.510
to re-engineer Canadians or Americans.

00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:10.260
The Netherlands and Germany have not fought
a war in more than 70 years.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:12.940
We did not have to genetically engineer the
Dutch.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:19.370
There are many changes to our institutions
and our norms and our ideas that can reduce

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:26.410
or eliminate the risks of nuclear war, without
what I consider a rather quixotic attempt

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:30.430
to change the course of human evolution.

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:35.900
Also on purely scientific grounds, I'm highly
sceptical of the prophesy that we will re-engineer

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:37.310
human nature.

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:43.490
I think that these predictions came during
the brief burst of enthusiasm for finding

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:48.510
the gene for intelligence, the gene for altruism
and so on.

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:54.350
We now know that there is no such gene; there
are hundreds or thousands of genes, each of

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:59.760
which increments or decrements psychological
traits by a tiny amount.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:03.540
To genetically engineer someone it's not a
matter of sticking in one gene, you'd have

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:05.530
to replace thousands of genes.

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:09.530
We have no idea how to do that; we're not
going to know how to do that any time soon,

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:16.170
and we also don't know how many of those genes
might lead to an improvement in one aspect

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:18.160
and a risk in another aspect.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:23.650
There may be a gene that increases your IQ
by two-thirds of a point, but also increases

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:27.920
your chances of getting brain cancer, or bipolar
disorder by a third of a point.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:36.730
It's going to be a very long time, if ever,
until we know how to balance those tiny benefits

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:41.120
and tiny risks, multiplied by hundreds or
thousands of genes.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:44.709
So on purely scientific grounds, I doubt that
it will happen, and on historical grounds,

00:02:44.709 --> 00:02:46.560
I don't think we need it.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:54.540
What will be your choice, what is it that
you think is essential to make sure that,

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:57.410
in whatever form 'we can save the world'?

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:01.599
First of all, we have to have an empirical
mindset.

00:03:01.599 --> 00:03:06.620
You are right: there are many hypotheses,
we have to look which ones have made the world

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:08.739
better and which have made the world worse.

00:03:08.739 --> 00:03:12.000
I think the track record of messiahs is not
particularly good.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.760
I think there is excellent reason to believe
that there is no such thing as a messiah,

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:16.890
and there never will be.

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:23.940
On the other hand, there are some things that
do work: international institutions like the

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:29.011
United Nations have decreased the probability
of war, it hasn't eliminated war but it has

00:03:29.011 --> 00:03:30.240
made it less likely.

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:38.150
We have reason to believe that trade and cosmopolitanism,
the movement of people and ideas, has been

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:39.190
a positive force.

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:44.420
We have reason to think that democracy has
more advantages than disadvantages, and I

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:50.030
think that what we have to do is not believe
that we can deduce what will make the world

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:56.440
better from first principles, and then impose
them in full confidence that we know how the

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:57.440
world is going to react.

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:59.590
Because we don't; we're not that smart.

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:01.361
But we really have to look at our past track
record.

00:04:01.361 --> 00:04:08.830
Look at the data: what makes people better
off, what makes people worse off?

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:13.630
The conference will be the weekend after the
American elections.

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:18.549
Will you still say the same things if Mr.
Trump will be the next president of America?

00:04:18.549 --> 00:04:22.650
I think it is extremely unlikely, and all
the indicators are that he will not be the

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.919
next president.

00:04:24.919 --> 00:04:29.259
If he is president, I think that would definitely
be a negative development, and there is no

00:04:29.259 --> 00:04:35.889
guarantee that all positive trends, such as
the trend towards tolerance, cosmopolitanism,

00:04:35.889 --> 00:04:40.750
democracy and knowledge-guided decision making
will continue.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:46.729
There are no iron laws that propel the world
in a particular direction.

00:04:46.729 --> 00:04:51.749
There are contingent events that are unpredictable,
so bad things could happen.

00:04:51.749 --> 00:04:56.930
How bad could it be if Trump were elected?

00:04:56.930 --> 00:05:03.869
Much depends on how much a single man can
control the entire apparatus of American government.

00:05:03.869 --> 00:05:09.680
Fortunately, American government has some
checks and balances built in; there's the

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:17.949
Supreme Court, there's the legislatures, there's
local governments and state governments, and

00:05:17.949 --> 00:05:23.400
the willingness or reluctance of the American
people to go along with a particular policy.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:29.069
So as long as Trump doesn't become the Führer,
or like Mao, with absolute control, and I

00:05:29.069 --> 00:05:33.830
think that's unlikely, then the worst-case
scenarios probably will not happen.

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:37.979
But then, Trump being elected is itself a
worst-case scenario, that I think will probably

00:05:37.979 --> 00:05:40.979
not happen.

